---
import baseline from "../../data/content-baseline.json";
import FlangeChecker from "./FlangeChecker.astro";
import ProcurementCtaTier from "./ProcurementCtaTier.astro";
const s=baseline.product.specifications;
const items=[
 ["The assembled pole","Provide the height, material and total assembled weight—including any luminaire, bracket, battery, solar panel or other attachment. A height alone does not establish the lifting conditions."],
 ["The flange and bolt drawing","Include flange dimensions, hole positions, hole sizes, plate thickness and anchor bolt specification. A dimensioned drawing is more useful than a description such as “standard base”."],
 ["The foundation arrangement","Identify the foundation type and how the pole is connected. Ground and anchor conditions must be reviewed; the equipment sheet does not establish a direct-burial solution."],
 ["The actual site","Share access, working space, surface conditions and any relevant site restrictions. The equipment needs a project-specific review rather than an assumption based on portability."],
 ["The project scope","Add the application, quantity and destination. If information is missing, say so: the inquiry can start before every drawing is ready."]
];
---
<main id="main"><div class="wrap"><p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Compatibility</p><div class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Project review guide</p><h1>A matching height<br/>isn't the whole picture.</h1><p class="lead muted">Use this guide to prepare a pole lifter compatibility review. It helps identify the information to send; it does not automatically approve a lifting operation.</p></div></div>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap two-column"><div><p class="eyebrow">Reference envelope</p><h2>Start with<br/>the listed specifications.</h2><p class="muted" style="margin-top:20px">The source sheet lists {s.applicablePoleHeightM} m light poles and a {s.ratedLoadKg} kg rated load. It also lists {s.listedAnchorBoltSizes.join(", ")}, with a flange hole span of {s.flangeHoleSpanMm.join("–")} mm.</p><p class="muted" style="margin-top:14px">These values are inputs to review. Pole geometry, assembled attachments and the connection arrangement still matter. Some flange-diagram terminology requires engineering clarification.</p><a class="text-link" style="margin-top:25px" href="/products/light-pole-jack/#specifications">Return to the full specification <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="yellow-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Important distinction</p><h3>Listed does not mean included.</h3><p>M16, M18, M20 and M22 are the bolt sizes in the standard included configuration. M24 is shown in the compatibility table and must be discussed separately.</p><p style="margin-top:20px">Site setup, anchoring, operator position and clearances need a reviewed operating manual. This guide is for project preparation.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;padding-bottom:20px"><div class="wrap"><FlangeChecker /></div></section>
  <section class="section dark-section"><div class="wrap section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Information to prepare</p><h2>Five pieces<br/>of the same picture.</h2></div><p class="muted">A clear drawing and a few project details make the initial review more useful. Unknown values can be left open for follow-up.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:20px"><div class="wrap two-column"><ol class="checklist">{items.map(([title,description])=><li><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></li>)}</ol><aside class="yellow-panel" style="position:sticky;top:25px"><p class="eyebrow">Your preparation checklist</p><h3>What do you have ready?</h3><form id="preparation-checklist"><div class="preparation-items">{items.map(([title],i)=><label><input type="checkbox" name={`ready-${i}`}/><span>{title}</span></label>)}</div><output aria-live="polite" id="preparation-status" data-ready-template="{count} of 5 information groups ready.">0 of 5 information groups ready.</output><p class="note">This measures information collected. It is not an equipment suitability verdict.</p><a class="button ink-button" style="margin-top:24px" href="/quote/">Send what you have <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></form></aside></div></section>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap"><ProcurementCtaTier highlightTier={3} /></div></section>
</main>
<style>.preparation-items{display:grid;gap:16px;margin:25px 0}.preparation-items label{display:flex;align-items:start;gap:12px;cursor:pointer}.preparation-items input{width:19px;height:19px;accent-color:#202622;flex-shrink:0}.preparation-items+output{font-size:13px;font-weight:600}@media(max-width:760px){aside{position:static!important}}</style>
<script>const form=document.getElementById("preparation-checklist"),output=document.getElementById("preparation-status");form?.addEventListener("change",()=>{const count=form.querySelectorAll("input:checked").length;if(output)output.textContent=(output.dataset.readyTemplate??"{count} of 5 information groups ready.").replace("{count}",String(count));});</script>
